==Summary==
* A new addon profiling API has been added.

==Resources==
* TOC: <code>110007</code>
* Official patch notes: [https://worldofwarcraft.blizzard.com/en-us/news/24165042#item10 Siren Isle Update Notes]
* Diffs: [https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/compare/11.0.5..11.0.7 wow-ui-source], [https://github.com/Ketho/BlizzardInterfaceResources/compare/11.0.5..11.0.7 BlizzardInterfaceResources]
* Deprecated API: [https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/11.0.7/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_Deprecated/Deprecated_11_0_7.lua Blizzard_Deprecated]

==Addon Profiling API==

A new C_AddOnProfiler namespace has been added with functions for querying CPU performance metrics associated with addons.

The measurements recorded by this new profiler are always enabled and do '''not''' require the [[CVar scriptProfile|scriptProfile]] CVar to be enabled. As with existing profiling functions, these APIs only return values for user-installed addons and cannot be used to query the performance of secure Blizzard addons, nor can they be used to measure the performance of macro commands such as [[MACRO run|/run]]. Metrics are reset with UI reloads.

* {{api|t=a|C_AddOnProfiler.GetAddOnMetric(name, metric)}} : <span class="apiret">result</span> - Returns a time value measured in milliseconds.
* {{api|t=a|C_AddOnProfiler.GetOverallMetric(metric)}} : <span class="apiret">result</span> - As above, but returned value is the sum across all loaded addons.
* {{api|t=a|C_AddOnProfiler.IsEnabled()}} : <span class="apiret">enabled</span> - Currently this function always returns true.

The metric parameter in the listed APIs corresponds to entries in [[Enum.AddOnProfilerMetric]], listed below.

{{:Enum.AddOnProfilerMetric}}

===Details===
See {{api|C_AddOnProfiler.GetAddOnMetric}} for implementation details, including how profiling blame is attributed.

==C_LFGList==
* {{api|t=a|C_LFGList.GetSearchResultInfo(searchResultID)}} - Changed <code>activityID</code> return field to <code>activityIDs</code>.

